        <headline>Storm Watch issued September 24 at 8:35AM EDT until September 26 at 6:00PM EDT by NWS Mount Holly NJ</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...For the Gale Warning, northeast winds 30 to 35 kt with
gusts up to 45 kt and seas 13 to 16 ft. For the Storm Watch,
north winds 30 to 40 kt with gusts up to 50 kt and seas 12 to
17 ft possible.

* WHERE...Waters from Sandy Hook NJ to Manasquan Inlet NJ from
20 to 40 NM, Waters from Manasquan Inlet NJ to Little Egg
Inlet NJ from 20 to 60 NM, Waters from Little Egg Inlet NJ to
Great Egg Inlet NJ from 20 to 60 NM, Waters from Great Egg
Inlet NJ to Cape May NJ from 20 to 60 NM and Waters from Cape
May NJ to Fenwick Island DE from 20 to 60 NM.

* WHEN...For the Gale Warning, until 6 AM EDT Friday. For the
Storm Watch, from Friday morning through Saturday afternoon.

* IMPACTS...Storm force winds and hazardous seas could capsize
or damage vessels and reduce visibility.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should prepare to remain in port, alter course, and/or
secure the vessel before the onset of severe conditions.</instruction>
